# Rank 1987 / CVE-2026-34723 (GHSA-hcm9-ch62-5727, CWE-284): once a Zammad
# system has more than two users, GET /api/v1/getting_started hands an
# unauthenticated caller the whole internal setup state. The action's own
# guard line is dead code for that path --
#
#   app/controllers/getting_started_controller.rb (parent of 9587452):
#     def index
#       return if setup_done_response          # renders + returns true first
#       return if auto_wizard_enabled_response
#       return if setup_done && !authentication_check   # unreachable when done
#       render json: { setup_done: setup_done, ... }
#     end
#
# because setup_done_response renders groups, email addresses, config and
# channel drivers whenever setup_done holds and returns true, so index
# returns before the authentication line runs. No before_action guards the
# action: the class declares `prepend_before_action -> { authorize! },
# only: [:base]`, and index/auto_wizard_admin are outside the only-list.
# Fix 9587452 moves the check into the render helper's gate,
# `return false if !setup_done || !authentication_check`, and deletes the
# dead line -- the helper renders only for authenticated callers and
# auto_wizard_admin inherits the same gate.
#
# What the scanner sees on the real file, both revisions identical:
#   - vyql match labels params -> code.HttpInput, Group.where /
#     EmailAddress.where -> code.DatabaseRead, and authorize! (line 4, the
#     class-body lambda) -> core.AuthorizationCheck. The render call is
#     unlabelled: the only Ruby render sink binding is gated on
#     dependency("rails"), and the SCA manifest table has no Gemfile reader
#     (internal/extract/sca/discover.go:14), so every dependency-gated Ruby
#     binding is inert on any tree -- the same family as the missing
#     Gradle/NuGet readers recorded for rank 1069, now with its Ruby
#     instance measured.
#   - No rule connects a database read to a render as a disclosure finding
#     in any language; DatabaseRead is a source only for stored-XSS and
#     stored-command rules.
#   - Bounded scans (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB, --cache off), three runs
#     per revision: app/controllers 127 findings, app/ 1086 findings, both
#     byte-identical across the fixed revisioned revision, and zero rows on
#     getting_started_controller.rb at either revision.
#
# Nothing is shippable here, measured:
#   - The fixed revision's only atoms are the project's own concern-method name. Every
#     other token in the file is identical across the revisions, so any
#     discriminating binding must key `authentication_check` --
#     ApplicationController::Authenticates' private method, not a library
#     API. Enumerated across every corpus clone, `authentication_check`
#     occurs in zammad alone (0 hits in vagrant, view_component and every
#     other Ruby tree); a binding keyed on it is inert everywhere else and
#     fails the genericity test outright.
#   - The generic form without project vocabulary -- a method that renders
#     model data with no authentication call in its own scope -- fires on
#     64 methods in 42 of zammad's 145 controller files (enumerated by
#     grep), because 101 of those controllers hang their auth on class-level
#     `prepend_before_action :authentication_check /
#     :authenticate_and_authorize!` wiring that a function scope cannot
#     see. Exactly one of the 64 is this CVE, and the shape reports the
#     patched revision identically: the endpoint-with-no-authorization-
#     signal variants measured to score the same on vulnerable and patched
#     trees (rank 1331), and the wiring-decided-authorization family
#     (ranks 1514, 1535, 1540, 1556, 1557, 1593).
#   - The documented-API counterweight does not exist: the guarded method
#     gains only the project-internal call; its other calls (render,
#     where, Setting.get) are present in both revisions.
#
# VYQL-AUTH-075 (code.PublicRestDataEndpointMissingAuthorization) is the
# concept this arrangement would light up if the vocabulary ever exists;
# both blocks pin the miss it reports nothing today.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1987: a setup-state-gated helper renders internal system state with no authentication in scope"
  lang ruby
  file getting_started_controller.rb
  reject VYQL-AUTH-075
  code
  ```
  class GettingStartedController < ApplicationController
    prepend_before_action -> { authorize! }, only: [:base]

    def index
      # check if first user exists
      return if setup_done_response

      # if admin user exists, we need to be authenticated
      return if setup_done && !authentication_check

      render json: {
        setup_done:  setup_done,
        import_mode: Setting.get('import_mode'),
      }
    end

    def base
      authorize!
      render json: { result: 'ok' }
    end

    private

    def setup_done
      User.count > 2
    end

    def setup_done_response
      return false if !setup_done

      groups = Group.where(active: true)
      addresses = EmailAddress.where(active: true)

      render json: {
        setup_done: true,
        addresses:  addresses,
        groups:     groups,
        config:     { product_logo: Setting.get('product_logo') },
      }
      true
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1987: the patched helper keeps the setup-state gate and adds the authentication gate"
  lang ruby
  file getting_started_controller.rb
  reject VYQL-AUTH-075
  code
  ```
  class GettingStartedController < ApplicationController
    prepend_before_action -> { authorize! }, only: [:base]

    def index
      # check if first user exists
      return if setup_done_response

      render json: {
        setup_done:  setup_done,
        import_mode: Setting.get('import_mode'),
      }
    end

    def base
      authorize!
      render json: { result: 'ok' }
    end

    private

    def setup_done
      User.count > 2
    end

    def setup_done_response
      return false if !setup_done || !authentication_check

      groups = Group.where(active: true)
      addresses = EmailAddress.where(active: true)

      render json: {
        setup_done: true,
        addresses:  addresses,
        groups:     groups,
        config:     { product_logo: Setting.get('product_logo') },
      }
      true
    end
  end
  ```
